  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah homeowners can finance a roof replacement through contractor payment plans, home equity loans, or government assistance programs with terms ranging from zero-down to 180 months.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "contractor payment plans, home equity loans, or government assistance programs"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Contractor Financing"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Many local roofing companies partner with third-party lenders to offer quick approvals and flexible payment structures right from their offices."
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Promotional Plans: Options often include \"Same-As-Cash\" periods with 0% interest for 6 to 12 months if paid in full."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fixed Rates: Standard monthly payment plans feature fixed APRs starting as low as 4.99% up to 11.99% with terms spanning 5 to 15 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "You can explore specific provider structures and soft credit pre-qualifications directly through Legacy Roofing or estimate monthly schedules via Whitaker Roofing .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Legacy Roofing",
                "link": "https://www.legacyroofingutah.com/financing"
              },
              {
                "text": "Whitaker Roofing",
                "link": "https://whitakerroofing.com/financing"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Home Equity Options (HELOCs)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you have built equity in your home, borrowing against it typically secures lower interest rates than unsecured personal loans."
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "HELOCs: Home equity lines of credit let you draw funds as needed for the project and can stretch repayment timelines up to 30 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Limits: These loans can cover larger amounts (up to $150,000) if you are upgrading to premium materials like metal or tile."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Government Assistance Programs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "USDA Section 504: Very-low-income rural homeowners who occupy their house can apply for the USDA Single Family Housing Repair Loans & Grants in Utah .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "USDA Single Family Housing Repair Loans & Grants in Utah",
                "link": "https://www.rd.usda.gov/programs-services/single-family-housing-programs/single-family-housing-repair-loans-grants/ut"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Grants: Homeowners aged 62 or older may qualify for direct grants to fix safety hazards like a leaking roof."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your estimated roof size or replacement cost"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are looking for low monthly payments or 0% interest promotional periods"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out which financing path fits your budget best."
      },
